recast disparity and flow as supervised regression (DispNet, FlowNet) and released FlyingThings3D, Monkaa, and Driving, the synthetic corpora that made this training regime possible. SENSE [] shares one encoder across disparity, optical flow, occlusion, and semantic heads; DRISF [] keeps the piecewise-rigid prior of Vogel et al. but implements it as an instance-level decoder over learned features. DRISF surpassed both listed variational baselines on KITTI Scene Flow, while SENSE improved on OSF but not PRSM (Table ), shifting the bottleneck from optimization to supervised data.

